    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d606">

                <pb facs="0730" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg688"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 10, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> In your note of the 17th of June last,
                    which has been received, your lordship inquires whether it would be agreeable to
                    this government if a proclamation should be made by the governor of British
                    Honduras, under the provisions of an act of the legislature of that colony,
                    declaring that Boston, New <pb facs="0731" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/> York, and
                    Philadelphia, are regarded as ports of emigration, with a view to canvass for an
                    emigration of colored laborers from the United States.</p>
                <p>Having taken the directions of the President, I have to inform your lordship that
                    this government interposes no objection to the voluntary immigration of persons
                    of the class described, and of course none to the proclamation proposed.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
